00:01:04.499 --> 00:01:05.332
We get older and...

00:01:05.332 --> 00:01:06.165
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:07.704
- New generations come
in and there's, you know

00:01:07.704 --> 00:01:08.675
they can be exposed to everything.

00:01:08.675 --> 00:01:09.508
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:09.508 --> 00:01:10.341
- Which is exciting.

00:01:10.341 --> 00:01:11.174
- Yeah.

00:01:11.174 --> 00:01:12.007
- [Alanis] Yeah.

00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:12.840
- But it's interesting.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.483
Do you find it interesting
how you write songs

00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:17.227
and it's coming from, I feel
like a lot yours are personal.

00:01:17.227 --> 00:01:18.060
- [Alanis] Mm, yeah.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:20.267
- And then people
perceive them differently?

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.100
Like I'll be in like a meet and greet.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:21.933
- Yes.

00:01:21.933 --> 00:01:22.766
- And I'll be like wait, what?

00:01:22.766 --> 00:01:24.259
And they'll think a song like I wrote.

00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:25.092
- The interpretation.

00:01:25.092 --> 00:01:25.925
- Yeah, the interpretation.

00:01:25.925 --> 00:01:26.758
- Yes. That happens a lot.

00:01:26.758 --> 00:01:28.976
I remember when I wrote a
song called "Hands Clean",

00:01:28.976 --> 00:01:30.954
someone came up to me and they said,

00:01:30.954 --> 00:01:32.995
I love that story you tell about this

00:01:32.995 --> 00:01:35.218
where you're in love with
your lesbian teacher.

00:01:35.218 --> 00:01:36.424
And that song is so beautiful.

00:01:36.424 --> 00:01:38.184
The dedication to her is so amazing.

00:01:38.184 --> 00:01:42.090
And I just thought, well,
which teacher was that?

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.152
- Did you then go, are you in love

00:01:44.152 --> 00:01:45.296
with your lesbian teacher?

00:01:45.296 --> 00:01:46.272
- [Alanis] Is there some
projection going on?

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.242
- Yeah, is there some projection,

00:01:47.242 --> 00:01:50.131
'cause that's...no one got that
from that, just that person.

00:01:50.131 --> 00:01:51.738
- But the point of it is just that once,

00:01:51.738 --> 00:01:53.170
I mean, when I write it for me,

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.739
it's beautifully self-indulgent
in a way that's important

00:01:55.739 --> 00:01:56.808
for artists to do, I think.

00:01:56.808 --> 00:01:57.641
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:57.641 --> 00:01:58.474
- And then once I share it

00:01:58.474 --> 00:01:59.907
it's yours to interpret as you wish.

00:01:59.907 --> 00:02:02.483
And I'm always charmed by
how people interpret it.

00:02:02.483 --> 00:02:04.619
'Cause it's no longer about
me once they're listening,

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:05.452
you know?

00:02:05.452 --> 00:02:06.285
- Yeah. 100%.

00:02:06.285 --> 00:02:07.118
- Yeah.

00:02:07.118 --> 00:02:08.154
- That was the coolest
part of your audience.

00:02:08.154 --> 00:02:10.571
Like, I was literally,
there was every age,

00:02:10.571 --> 00:02:12.659
every walk of life, every, like,

00:02:12.659 --> 00:02:13.498
coming to your show is like

00:02:13.498 --> 00:02:14.331
- [Alanis] Humans. Yes.

00:02:14.331 --> 00:02:16.674
- When would we all be in
this one place at one time?

00:02:16.674 --> 00:02:17.719
- Isn't it amazing?

00:02:17.719 --> 00:02:20.899
- Like, it was, it's cool
though, how far you touch people.

00:02:20.899 --> 00:02:23.891
Like, how, that broad, you
know, one of the best albums

00:02:23.891 --> 00:02:26.715
of all time and so many great songs.

00:02:26.715 --> 00:02:28.539
But I love, I was gonna,
I'm skipping ahead

00:02:28.539 --> 00:02:29.571
because I'm ADHD.

00:02:29.571 --> 00:02:30.404
- Oh, you can.

00:02:30.404 --> 00:02:32.024
- But it's because you
said it's how you feel

00:02:32.024 --> 00:02:33.019
like, in music,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.112
and I love that you did
this meditation album

00:02:35.112 --> 00:02:37.683
because you're known for lyrics right?

00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:38.994
Or for my world you are.

00:02:38.994 --> 00:02:39.827
- Yeah.

00:02:39.827 --> 00:02:42.218
- And I think it's beautiful
the fact that you're now,

00:02:42.218 --> 00:02:43.395
there's no lyrics, right?

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:44.228
- [Alanis] Right.

00:02:44.228 --> 00:02:45.314
- It's all like medita-
it's been hard couple years.

00:02:45.314 --> 00:02:46.296
- Yes. Yes.

00:02:46.296 --> 00:02:48.283
- [Kelly] For a lot of us so, or everyone.

00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:49.416
- Yeah.

00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:51.851
- And it's, was that why
you decided to do it?

00:02:51.851 --> 00:02:53.271
Because there's no lyrics,
but it's still like very,

00:02:53.271 --> 00:02:54.363
it's you.

00:02:54.363 --> 00:02:56.611
- It's an invitation to feel, basically.

00:02:56.611 --> 00:02:57.444
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:57.444 --> 00:03:00.210
- And what I consider it in
terms of it being different

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.763
from meditation records that I adore

00:03:01.763 --> 00:03:04.579
is that there's an invitation
to feel different things.

00:03:04.579 --> 00:03:05.867
You don't have to just be zenned out

00:03:05.867 --> 00:03:08.521
to listen to meditation music
in this particular case.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.354
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:09.354 --> 00:03:12.898
- There's mania and there's
rage and there's release

00:03:12.898 --> 00:03:13.819
and there's fear.

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:15.481
And you know, I mean,
so much was going on.

00:03:15.481 --> 00:03:17.691
I mean, our whole lives
there's so much going on,

00:03:17.691 --> 00:03:19.275
I can't believe we're all still here. But.

00:03:19.275 --> 00:03:20.108
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:20.108 --> 00:03:22.475
- Those two years in
particular, the lockdown eras,

00:03:22.475 --> 00:03:24.611
I just kept thinking.

00:03:24.611 --> 00:03:26.121
I was so inspired to begin with,

00:03:26.121 --> 00:03:27.867
but I didn't wanna write a
record that was, you know,

00:03:27.867 --> 00:03:30.931
beautifully naval gazing as
artists really need to do

00:03:30.931 --> 00:03:32.211
I think.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:33.067
- Yeah.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.265
- So I wanted to create something

00:03:34.265 --> 00:03:37.680
that would be helpful for
me in my meditative process,

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.223
but also would be a gift
on some level to people

00:03:41.223 --> 00:03:43.617
if they want to use it
as a tool or a companion,

00:03:43.617 --> 00:03:47.267
because sometimes when I'm in
a trauma or I'm in a flashback

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.115
or whatever I'm in.

00:03:48.115 --> 00:03:48.948
- [Kelly] Yeah, you're triggered.

00:03:48.948 --> 00:03:52.347
- Meditating is actually
just kind of re-traumatizing

00:03:52.347 --> 00:03:53.180
in some ways.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.881
There's this meditative induced
anxiety that can come up

00:03:56.881 --> 00:03:58.816
for those of us who are
protected a lot of times.

00:03:58.816 --> 00:04:00.187
Meditating can be too vulnerable.

00:04:00.187 --> 00:04:01.971
- Yeah. Like being still is like, yeah.

00:04:01.971 --> 00:04:03.873
- And hearing the voices
extra loud in your head

00:04:03.873 --> 00:04:04.872
is not always ideal.

00:04:04.872 --> 00:04:05.705
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:05.705 --> 00:04:08.520
- So sometimes music can be
a sort of gateway into it.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.721
You feel safe, compatriotised,
and healing, yeah.

00:04:11.721 --> 00:04:13.723
- Yeah. And I think that's magical, but.

00:04:13.723 --> 00:04:14.556
- [Alanis] Thanks.

00:04:14.556 --> 00:04:16.082
- Your dad gave you some advice,

00:04:16.082 --> 00:04:18.714
and I love this 'cause it
feels like you grew up in Texas

00:04:18.714 --> 00:04:19.547
with this advice.

00:04:19.547 --> 00:04:21.538
So, tell everybody what that advice is

00:04:21.538 --> 00:04:22.665
and how it's helped you.

00:04:22.665 --> 00:04:24.734
- Yes. So when I was, as I was
stepping into the public eye

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:26.306
as a young creature, my dad said,

00:04:26.306 --> 00:04:28.608
honey, there's gonna be three
ways people perceive you.

00:04:28.608 --> 00:04:31.074
He said, the first group
of people will adore you

00:04:31.074 --> 00:04:32.666
and you can do no wrong.

00:04:32.666 --> 00:04:34.522
The second group of people will hate you

00:04:34.522 --> 00:04:35.498
and you can do no right.

00:04:35.498 --> 00:04:36.331
- [Kelly] No matter what you do, yeah.

00:04:36.331 --> 00:04:38.242
- And then the third group of
people won't give a (beep).

00:04:38.242 --> 00:04:40.674
(everyone laughing)

00:04:40.674 --> 00:04:41.507
- I love that!

00:04:41.507 --> 00:04:43.050
- And he said, that'll be
the case no matter what,

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.447
so enjoy.

00:04:44.447 --> 00:04:46.186
- Yeah. No, but it's so freeing!

00:04:46.186 --> 00:04:47.019
- [Alanis] And it's true!

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:49.345
- It's liberating to know
that no matter what I do,

00:04:49.345 --> 00:04:51.086
no matter how people
pleasey I can be or...

00:04:51.086 --> 00:04:51.919
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:51.919 --> 00:04:53.518
- Fear of rejection or please like me,

00:04:53.518 --> 00:04:55.944
that no matter what, there's just no way.

00:04:55.944 --> 00:04:56.777
- Yeah.

00:04:56.777 --> 00:04:58.146
- I haven't read a comment about me

00:04:58.146 --> 00:05:01.423
that is disparaging and cruel in 20 years.

00:05:01.423 --> 00:05:03.226
- Oh my God! So I don't,
I don't do it either.

00:05:03.226 --> 00:05:04.146
I think it's so,

00:05:04.146 --> 00:05:06.776
'cause either you're gonna
wanna crawl in a hole and die.

00:05:06.776 --> 00:05:07.609
- Right.

00:05:07.609 --> 00:05:09.257
- Or you're gonna drink your own Kool-Aid,

00:05:09.257 --> 00:05:10.090
and we've met them.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:10.923
- Or you can drink.

00:05:10.923 --> 00:05:11.801
- Those people. Yeah.

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:13.562
Or you drink... to escape.

00:05:13.562 --> 00:05:14.970
- [Alanis] Yes. Yes. The pain.

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.081
- No, but it's, it's like it's,

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:17.113
or you drink your own Kool-Aid

00:05:17.113 --> 00:05:18.640
and you think like nothing
you do is like whatever.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.570
- Yeah, it's not that either.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.439
- [Kelly] So it's nothing is
good. No good comes from it.

00:05:21.439 --> 00:05:22.681
- Well, I think it's about soliciting

00:05:22.681 --> 00:05:25.874
someone's supportive
opinion who knows you.

00:05:25.874 --> 00:05:28.114
I'd rather have someone know me well

00:05:28.114 --> 00:05:30.346
and tell me what my growth edge might be

00:05:30.346 --> 00:05:31.950
and have them invite me into some behavior

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.257
that might be a little terrifying.

00:05:33.257 --> 00:05:34.090
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.944
- You know, and everyone
has their own growth edge.

00:05:35.944 --> 00:05:37.506
One person, it might be to show up more,

00:05:37.506 --> 00:05:40.574
another person it might be to
say no more often, you know.

00:05:40.574 --> 00:05:41.407
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:42.693
Hey!

00:05:42.693 --> 00:05:43.592
- Hey, yeah ha.

00:05:43.592 --> 00:05:44.687
Thank you. Wow.

00:05:44.687 --> 00:05:46.502
- I'm like, I feel you.

00:05:46.502 --> 00:05:48.352
So, I'm curious.

00:05:48.352 --> 00:05:50.718
Like, what was the first
album you bought as a kid?

00:05:50.718 --> 00:05:52.128
- "The Smurfs All Star Show".

00:05:52.128 --> 00:05:53.128
- The Smurfs. Yes!

00:05:53.128 --> 00:05:54.368
(everyone laughing)

00:05:54.368 --> 00:05:55.201
- So hip.

00:05:55.201 --> 00:05:56.757
- They escaped quite a bit.

00:05:56.757 --> 00:05:58.024
I feel like whoever invented this...

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:58.857
- They escaped a lot.

00:05:58.857 --> 00:05:59.992
- Yeah. I feel like The Smurfs too.

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:01.784
I feel like whoever created
that, they were on something.

00:06:01.784 --> 00:06:02.617
- [Alanis] Shrooms.

00:06:02.617 --> 00:06:04.157
- It was an interesting idea.

00:06:04.157 --> 00:06:05.728
It was like "Alice in Wonderland"-ish.

00:06:05.728 --> 00:06:06.734
I was like, what's happening?

00:06:06.734 --> 00:06:07.884
- Yes. And super diverse. It was cool.

00:06:07.884 --> 00:06:10.278
- Yeah. I'm just curious,
like who inspired you?

00:06:10.278 --> 00:06:11.135
'Cause well done.

00:06:11.135 --> 00:06:11.980
- Aw.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.072
- Whoever did.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:14.247
- I mean, so many people.

00:06:14.247 --> 00:06:16.302
Standing on the shoulders
of giants every day.

00:06:16.302 --> 00:06:18.424
I'm just constantly
blown away at the paper.

00:06:18.424 --> 00:06:20.008
- Everything you say sounds like it came

00:06:20.008 --> 00:06:21.799
