said. I just feel blessed.

00:06:48.816 --> 00:06:49.776
I'm like, wait, what?

00:06:49.776 --> 00:06:50.609
- You're killing me.

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:51.472
- Alchemy of your, I was like, what?

00:06:51.472 --> 00:06:54.869
So, you're currently touring
and like I was telling y'all,

00:06:54.869 --> 00:06:58.728
I'm not kidding, it's literally
possibly my favorite show

00:06:58.728 --> 00:06:59.984
I've ever been to in my life.

00:06:59.984 --> 00:07:01.968
Like, it was just so good.

00:07:01.968 --> 00:07:04.748
And do you, I was just
wondering, because everyone,

00:07:04.748 --> 00:07:06.040
you are such a lyric person.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.231
Do you ever forget them
and just make them up?

00:07:08.231 --> 00:07:09.064
I do.

00:07:09.064 --> 00:07:09.897
- Of course.

00:07:09.897 --> 00:07:10.730
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.632
- Yes. Or there have been
moments where I'm singing

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:15.175
and thank the Lord, the
audience knows the lyrics,

00:07:15.175 --> 00:07:16.015
and I'll just do that.

00:07:16.015 --> 00:07:16.848
- You sing.

00:07:16.848 --> 00:07:17.681
- Yeah.

00:07:17.681 --> 00:07:18.514
- Yeah.

00:07:18.514 --> 00:07:20.432
'Cause I'm like, am I in
the second verse? Yeah.

00:07:20.432 --> 00:07:21.776
I'm like, wait, what? I'm like, yeah.

00:07:21.776 --> 00:07:22.609
- Yes.

00:07:22.609 --> 00:07:23.615
- 'Cause sometimes, yeah.

00:07:23.615 --> 00:07:25.733
- No, I mean it completely disappears.

00:07:25.733 --> 00:07:26.912
- Yes. Okay.

00:07:26.912 --> 00:07:27.951
- That happens, that's so normal.

00:07:27.951 --> 00:07:28.784
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:07:28.784 --> 00:07:29.617
- Yes.

00:07:29.617 --> 00:07:30.450
- I just have you here
to make me feel normal.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.384
- Okay good. My joy is to do that.

00:07:32.384 --> 00:07:33.432
- This is actually interesting

00:07:33.432 --> 00:07:35.846
because when this next artist,
when I heard her record,

00:07:35.846 --> 00:07:39.096
Olivia Rodrigo, I literally
told all of y'all.

00:07:39.096 --> 00:07:40.086
(audience cheering)

00:07:40.086 --> 00:07:45.086
And I literally said she...
y'all are very different artists

00:07:45.488 --> 00:07:48.967
but I listened to her
album from beginning to end

00:07:48.967 --> 00:07:52.207
and I was like, I'm 40,
and I'm really into this.

00:07:52.207 --> 00:07:54.424
And I was like, and it's so good.

00:07:54.424 --> 00:07:59.239
And I feel like it's like a
different version of like you.

00:07:59.239 --> 00:08:00.440
Like, I feel like y'all are very similar.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.294
I feel like you're different.

00:08:01.294 --> 00:08:02.127
- Yeah.

00:08:02.127 --> 00:08:03.024
- [Kelly] But I thought, man.

00:08:03.024 --> 00:08:03.857
- Similar fabric.

00:08:03.857 --> 00:08:06.168
- She had to have been, like,
influenced by you a bit.

00:08:06.168 --> 00:08:07.925
'Cause it's, I feel
like she was that artist

00:08:07.925 --> 00:08:10.029
that I feel like for her
generation was, like,

00:08:10.029 --> 00:08:11.744
my generation's Alanis.

00:08:11.744 --> 00:08:14.743
And so, is it true that
you gave her, I heard,

00:08:14.743 --> 00:08:16.816
some kind of survival,
like road survival kit?

00:08:16.816 --> 00:08:18.520
- She mentioned she was going on the road

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:21.040
and hadn't done that a lot
and I just thought, oh, okay.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:21.873
- Your voice is gonna die.

00:08:21.873 --> 00:08:23.640
- Well, yeah. And then
also there's sort of,

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.808
archetypally, constitutionally,

00:08:25.808 --> 00:08:27.719
you're either kind of a
road dog or you're not.

00:08:27.719 --> 00:08:28.552
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:28.552 --> 00:08:29.768
- And I think those of
us who are road dogs,

00:08:29.768 --> 00:08:31.112
we have little tricks up our sleeve

00:08:31.112 --> 00:08:33.791
of what to bring to
survive, for self care even.

00:08:33.791 --> 00:08:35.655
So for me, it's about, you know,

00:08:35.655 --> 00:08:38.375
bringing the equivalent of
my blankie everywhere I go,

00:08:38.375 --> 00:08:39.208
you know?

00:08:39.208 --> 00:08:40.041
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:40.041 --> 00:08:40.912
- It's as simple as a pillow or...

00:08:40.912 --> 00:08:41.745
- [Kelly] Your comforts, yeah.

00:08:41.745 --> 00:08:43.840
- Yeah. And so I think I
mentioned in our conversation,

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.256
Olivia's and my conversation

00:08:45.256 --> 00:08:47.407
that I would send her a care package

00:08:47.407 --> 00:08:48.600
and I really should get on that.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:49.600
- You should really (laughs)

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:51.008
- Yeah. Thanks for reminding me, Kelly.

00:08:51.008 --> 00:08:51.841
- Yes.

00:08:51.841 --> 00:08:52.974
- But I will and I can, yeah.

00:08:52.974 --> 00:08:54.517
- No, it's just interesting

00:08:54.517 --> 00:08:57.232
because I've never compared anyone to you.

00:08:57.232 --> 00:08:59.880
And I was just like, wow,
she's like a younger version,

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.680
like a different version or whatever.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.656
But anyway, so what will be
in it? What's in your comfort?

00:09:05.656 --> 00:09:08.592
Do you have a blankie,
Linus? Like, you do?

00:09:08.592 --> 00:09:09.456
- Anything cozy.

00:09:09.456 --> 00:09:10.289
- Okay.

00:09:10.289 --> 00:09:12.400
- At our house anywhere
you fall it's a mattress

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.272
or a cozy blanket.

00:09:13.272 --> 00:09:14.830
I think I have that the hygge.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:17.960
The huga, it's actually
pronounced, H Y G G E.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:18.847
- [Kelly] What's that?

00:09:18.847 --> 00:09:20.688
- Danish. It's sort of a cozy,

00:09:20.688 --> 00:09:22.216
it's commitment to cozy basically.

00:09:22.216 --> 00:09:23.049
- Okay.

00:09:23.049 --> 00:09:23.882
- I'm Crasley.

00:09:23.882 --> 00:09:24.983
- Even your blankets are cool.

00:09:24.983 --> 00:09:25.992
What?

00:09:25.992 --> 00:09:28.762
I'm like, mine was like target
or something, I don't know.

00:09:28.762 --> 00:09:29.952
- [Alanis] Oh, probably cool.

00:09:29.952 --> 00:09:30.785
- Yeah.

00:09:30.785 --> 00:09:32.640
- No, I'm obsessed with
the idea of creating

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:34.400
any semblance of comfort on the road.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:37.659
So it could be essential oil
sprays, meditation music.

00:09:37.659 --> 00:09:38.997
I always have these mini altars

00:09:38.997 --> 00:09:42.147
I throw together at the last second.

00:09:42.147 --> 00:09:44.013
For her, let's think
what we would give her.

00:09:44.013 --> 00:09:45.141
I mean, what would we give
her, Kelly, for survival?

00:09:45.141 --> 00:09:46.029
- Wait, I have question.

00:09:46.029 --> 00:09:46.862
So why do you, so like,
the mini altar situation,

00:09:46.862 --> 00:09:50.261
is it because it makes
you feel like tranquil?

00:09:50.261 --> 00:09:51.237
Is that, is it?

00:09:51.237 --> 00:09:53.213
- Yeah. And it's an invitation for ritual

00:09:53.213 --> 00:09:55.165
and actually breathing most of my life

00:09:55.165 --> 00:09:56.908
because of anxiety and all the feelings.

00:09:56.908 --> 00:09:57.741
- [Kelly] I think it's so important.

00:09:57.741 --> 00:09:59.773
- I, you know, I basically
have had a shallow breath,

00:09:59.773 --> 00:10:02.237
which sends a message to your
brain that you're in danger

00:10:02.237 --> 00:10:04.229
and that a Saber-toothed
tiger is coming right at you.

00:10:04.229 --> 00:10:05.062
- Yeah.

00:10:05.062 --> 00:10:05.895
- Which it isn't.

00:10:05.895 --> 00:10:06.728
- Yeah.

00:10:06.728 --> 00:10:07.561
- But it sure feels like it is.

00:10:07.561 --> 00:10:08.394
- Yeah.

00:10:08.394 --> 00:10:10.853
- So basically the only thing
that actually keeps me going

00:10:10.853 --> 00:10:11.686
is being hyper present,

00:10:11.686 --> 00:10:13.347
to the point where my
husband sometimes just goes,

00:10:13.347 --> 00:10:15.419
can we talk about the
future for five seconds?

00:10:15.419 --> 00:10:16.252
- Five seconds?

00:10:16.252 --> 00:10:17.085
- Yeah.

00:10:17.085 --> 00:10:18.027
- Oh my God, I'm your husband.

00:10:18.027 --> 00:10:18.860
- Oh!

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:19.693
- I'm a planner.

00:10:19.693 --> 00:10:21.925
I just like some kind of dream out there.

00:10:21.925 --> 00:10:24.306
I love you so much, it's
always great to see you

00:10:24.306 --> 00:10:25.139
- Aww, you too Kelly.

00:10:25.139 --> 00:10:25.972
- Thank you so much for coming by.

00:10:25.972 --> 00:10:26.805
- You're amazing. Thank you.

00:10:26.805 --> 00:10:27.796
- I love the new album,
I think it's so cool.

00:10:27.796 --> 00:10:28.868
- Thank you.

00:10:28.868 --> 00:10:30.289
- And it's so you, and
it's so gonna help us.

00:10:30.289 --> 00:10:31.532
- Oh, awesome.

00:10:31.532 --> 00:10:34.280
- So Alanis's meditation album,
"The Storm Before The Calm",

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:35.666
which is the raddest title ever,

00:10:35.666 --> 00:10:37.804
is available now for pre-order

00:10:37.804 --> 00:10:39.620
and out everywhere on June 17th.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.083
You can also catch her on
the "Jagged Little Pill"

00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:44.468
25th Anniversary Tour if you're smart.

00:10:44.468 --> 00:10:45.531
You really need to go,

00:10:45.531 --> 00:10:46.964
'cause Jessie's just pointing at herself.

00:10:46.964 --> 00:10:48.948
We had the best time ever.

